<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">bash</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">bash</ansi> command performs a shield bash attack during combat, using
your shield as a weapon to damage and potentially knock your opponent
to the ground.

<ansi fg="yellow">Requirements:</ansi>

  - Must be in active combat
  - Must have a shield equipped
  - Cannot be used if special move cooldown is active

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">bash</ansi>
  Bash your current combat target with your shield

<ansi fg="yellow">Mechanics:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">Damage:</ansi> Solid but not as heavy as a full weapon swing — the
    goal is the knockdown, not the wound.
  <ansi fg="stat">Knockdown Chance:</ansi> Decent, resolved against the defender's
    Dexterity and combat skill. Not as reliable as trip, but
    you hit harder getting there.
    - Attacker: Weapon Combat skill + Strength
    - Defender: Combat skill + Dexterity
  <ansi fg="stat">Cooldown:</ansi> Shared with trip and kick.
  <ansi fg="stat">Skill:</ansi> Progresses Weapon Combat

If the knockdown succeeds, your target becomes <ansi fg="red">prone</ansi> for a short
time, suffering attack and defense penalties. See
<ansi fg="command">help prone</ansi> for details.

<ansi fg="yellow">See Also:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">help trip</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help kick</ansi>,
